WireTuner: keep FreeHand's explicit "None" in property lists (the FreeHand importer, D-083).
- _readPropLstElements dropped every element whose value record is 0.  A FreeHand 9 or later
  object whose stroke or fill is set to None over its style's writes that key with the value 0
  (an ElemPropLst whose parent StylePropLst holds the stroke), so dropping it gave the object the
  style's stroke: a rectangle drawn with no fill and no stroke came in with the Normal style's
  1 pt black stroke.  The entry is kept with its 0; libfreehand's own lookups of value 0 find no
  record and draw nothing, and the importer reads it as None.

diff -ruN a/libfreehand/src/lib/FHParser.cpp b/libfreehand/src/lib/FHParser.cpp
--- a/libfreehand/src/lib/FHParser.cpp	2026-10-01 17:43:43
+++ b/libfreehand/src/lib/FHParser.cpp	2026-10-01 17:43:43
@@ -2770,7 +2770,9 @@
   {
     unsigned nameId = _readRecordId(input);
     unsigned valueId = _readRecordId(input);
-    if (nameId && valueId)
+    // WireTuner: a zero value is kept -- it is FreeHand's explicit "None" (an object whose
+    // stroke or fill is set to None over its style's), which dropping turned into the style's.
+    if (nameId)
       properties[nameId] = valueId;
   }
 }
